1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,377
<i>Are you going to file a case?</i>

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:03,670
<i>Yes, Auntie.</i>

3
00:00:03,753 --> 00:00:06,172
<i>If he doesn't leave me</i>
<i>and my brother alone.</i>

4
00:00:06,256 --> 00:00:09,426
<i>You had a lot of jobs</i>
<i>in Canada, Mr. Dominguez.</i>

5
00:00:09,509 --> 00:00:11,720
<i>You can start today, Mr. Dominguez.</i>

6
00:00:11,803 --> 00:00:12,929
[ENRICO]<i> Thank you.</i>
<i>Thank you, ma'am.</i>

7
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:14,055
<i>That's enough!</i>

8
00:00:14,139 --> 00:00:15,390
<i>- Sorry! Sorry!</i>
<i>- Let's go!</i>

9
00:00:15,473 --> 00:00:17,225
<i>Thank you, sir. I'm Oliver.</i>

10
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:19,227
<i>Oliver? Oh, Oliver!</i>

11
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:20,353
[PRECIOUS] <i>What happened?</i>

12
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:23,064
[ABI]<i> What I need is</i>
<i>another source of income.</i>

13
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:24,983
<i>Ms. Billy, maybe…?</i>

14
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:28,194
<i>The matchmaking feature slows down</i>
<i>during peak traffic hours.</i>

15
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:29,654
<i>What would you do?</i>

16
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:30,947
<i>Check the server first.</i>

17
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:33,241
<i>Or you can go straight to</i>
<i>enabling auto-scaling.</i>

18
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:34,784
<i>I would check the server first.</i>

19
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:37,328
<i>Or we can go straight to</i>
<i>enabling auto-scaling</i>

20
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:39,539
<i>so it can keep up with the traffic spike.</i>

21
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:41,124
[BILLY]<i> I know you had</i>
<i>a bad feeling about her.</i>

22
00:00:41,207 --> 00:00:42,584
<i>Now is your chance…</i>

23
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:45,754
[CHARM] <i>To prove I'm onto something.</i>

24
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:49,799
This one's on me, okay?

25
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:51,760
I'm treating you because

26
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:53,636
I can feel it.

27
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,639
I'm finally going to become
an office girl.

28
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:59,350
I'm going to be part
of the LoveList family.

29
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:01,186
And it's all because of you.

30
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:02,979
Anything for you.

31
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:06,649
Just one date with you is enough for me.

32
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:09,986
We're far away from them.

33
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:11,654
Why'd you bring me here?

34
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:13,281
You wanted me all to yourself, didn't you?

35
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:15,825
- All to myself?
- Oh, didn't you?

36
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:17,660
Of course I'm being careful.

37
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:20,121
What if someone recognizes us?

38
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:24,501
It's okay.

39
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:26,503
I know you're embarrassed
to be seen with me.

40
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:28,296
- This isn't even a date!
- It's okay!

41
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:29,714
It isn't! You're so stubborn.

42
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:34,135
I just wanted to thank you

43
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:35,512
for helping me.

44
00:01:35,595 --> 00:01:36,429
That's all.

45
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:37,889
I'm kidding.

46
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:39,349
You're way too serious.

47
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:41,226
Hey, but Caloy,

48
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:43,311
your situation isn't
something to joke about.

49
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:46,731
I'm about to become part of LoveList.

50
00:01:46,815 --> 00:01:50,151
But you've still got a case to face.

51
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:52,445
When are you and Jordan meeting?

52
00:01:52,529 --> 00:01:56,032
When's the preliminary investigation?

53
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:57,158
In a week.

54
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:01,287
Hey, not here.

55
00:02:02,997 --> 00:02:04,666
Not here. There are too many people.

56
00:02:04,749 --> 00:02:05,834
It's too early for that…

57
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:10,046
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

58
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:12,173
I knew it. You brought something again.

59
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:13,925
Honestly, you're unbelievable.

60
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:16,594
Hey! Why'd you throw it?!

61
00:02:16,678 --> 00:02:18,513
That's expensive!

62
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:20,056
You should try a different approach.

63
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:21,266
What kind of approach?

64
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:23,726
You know, like…

65
00:02:25,019 --> 00:02:26,354
being the good guy.

66
00:02:26,437 --> 00:02:27,981
Why don't you try that?

67
00:02:28,064 --> 00:02:32,026
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

68
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:33,194
[MUSIC FADES]

69
00:02:34,445 --> 00:02:39,826
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

70
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,952
AGREED! BRANDON'S
TOTAL HUSBAND MATERIAL.

71
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:24,621
PLUS, HE'S A TOTAL HOTTIE.

72
00:03:24,704 --> 00:03:26,372
DON'T LET HIM GET AWAY.

73
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:28,207
GO FOR IT, AUNTIE!

74
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,294
[PHONE RINGING]

75
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:33,379
Hello, Charm.

76
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:36,216
Did you check Abi's references?

77
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:38,885
Mm-hmm. Okay.

78
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:40,094
Let's talk later.

79
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:41,638
Thank you.

80
00:03:43,181 --> 00:03:44,349
Hmm…

81
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:48,603
I hope you hire Abi.

82
00:03:48,686 --> 00:03:50,813
I really do want to help her, Auntie Pres.

83
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:52,815
But of course, we have to
follow the proper process.

84
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:54,150
Hmm.

85
00:03:55,109 --> 00:03:56,945
- Three? That's a lot.
- Mm-hmm.

86
00:03:57,028 --> 00:03:58,905
This one, this one, and this one.

87
00:03:58,988 --> 00:04:00,573
Your brother asked for more.

88
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:02,533
- Oh?
- Yeah.

89
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:06,579
- One's for me.
- Okay.

90
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:08,498
- One's for Suzie.
- Okay.

91
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:10,833
And this one's for Sir Eric.

92
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:12,627
Sir Eric?

93
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:17,090
The meals should ideally
be ready by 9:00 a.m.

94
00:04:17,173 --> 00:04:19,342
Don't worry, ma'am.
The kitchen works fast.

95
00:04:19,425 --> 00:04:23,179
And I've already included
the healthier options I suggested.

96
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:25,306
Whole grains, low-sugar snacks…

97
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:26,641
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

98
00:04:26,724 --> 00:04:29,519
And, ma'am, could I get
the children's general records?

99
00:04:29,602 --> 00:04:31,980
- Their health profiles.
- Mm-hmm.

100
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:33,231
Then we can conduct a survey

101
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:35,149
to find out if anyone
has allergies we should avoid.

102
00:04:35,775 --> 00:04:38,611
I definitely made the right choice
hiring you, Mr. Dominguez.

103
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:41,906
Oh, he's the new canteen manager, Billy.

104
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:43,408
He's like an angel.

105
00:04:43,491 --> 00:04:44,659
- Hmm…
- You know…

106
00:04:44,742 --> 00:04:46,327
he stood up for me.

107
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:49,539
Biboy and his friends
were about to pick on me again.

108
00:04:49,622 --> 00:04:51,040
Is that so?

109
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:52,208
All right.

110
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,126
It's still early.

111
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:54,377
I'll drop you off.

112
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,712
Oh, no, no, no.

113
00:04:55,795 --> 00:04:57,630
Auntie Pres, I just want to thank…

114
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:59,132
- …his guardian angel.
- Oh.

115
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:00,758
- Come on.
- Okay.

116
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:02,343
Mm-hmm.

117
00:05:02,427 --> 00:05:05,138
- All right, let's go!
- Okay.

118
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:06,931
- Take care.
- Bye!

119
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:09,100
- Don't forget your kiss!
- Bye, Auntie Pres!

120
00:05:09,183 --> 00:05:11,519
- Behave!
- She said behave!

121
00:05:11,602 --> 00:05:13,146
- I meant you.
- Oh, me?

122
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:14,314
- Yes, you.
- I will.

123
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:15,732
Oh, by the way,

124
00:05:15,815 --> 00:05:17,650
did you already process
your police clearance?

125
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:20,320
Uh, I tried to.

126
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:22,739
But I got there after the cutoff.

127
00:05:22,822 --> 00:05:24,866
- Oh.
- Can I submit it next week?

128
00:05:24,949 --> 00:05:27,035
All right. Next week it is.

129
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:29,620
How are you doing there?

130
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,168
[WOMAN] Good morning, Ma'am Blaire.

131
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:37,295
Good morning. How are you doing?

132
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:42,216
Oh, Abi, you're here. Do you have
an appointment with our chief?

133
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,926
Oh, no, I don't.

134
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:46,888
Ms. Billy Idol
still hasn't gotten back to me

135
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:48,723
about my application.

136
00:05:48,806 --> 00:05:50,683
I just wanted to ask for an update.

137
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:53,478
Really? Do you want me
to give her a call instead?

138
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:55,688
Oh no, don't.
But she's coming in today, right?

139
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:58,816
Yes, she is.
She has a meeting this morning at eight.

140
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,443
Oh, okay. I'll just wait then.

141
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:02,862
- Okay, good luck.
- Thank you.

142
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:10,828
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

143
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:15,666
You're not applying for
an assistant position, are you?

144
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:16,918
Oh, no!

145
00:06:17,001 --> 00:06:18,878
Oh, okay. Just making sure.

146
00:06:18,961 --> 00:06:20,797
Mm-hmm. I'm applying
for a higher position.

147
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,258
- A higher position?
- Yes.

148
00:06:25,176 --> 00:06:26,803
This high? Huh?

149
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:28,930
[CHUCKLES] You're funny.

150
00:06:29,013 --> 00:06:31,307
- [CHUCKLES]
- That's just how I am.

151
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:32,475
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

152
00:06:32,558 --> 00:06:34,102
Uh, you look beautiful today.

153
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:36,646
Can I just wait inside?

154
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:39,315
Sure. Come on in.

155
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:40,983
Thank you. [CHUCKLES]

156
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:47,657
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

157
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:54,330
Hey, why are you following me?

158
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:55,957
Uh, where am I supposed to go?

159
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,583
Just stay here, okay?

160
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:59,252
Don't go upstairs yet.

161
00:06:59,335 --> 00:07:01,379
You're not that high up yet.

162
00:07:01,462 --> 00:07:02,713
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

163
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,389
Uh, miss? One coffee, please.

164
00:07:11,472 --> 00:07:13,683
- Okay, it'll be ready in a bit.
- Thank you.

165
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:15,059
[WOMAN] There, sent.

166
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:16,811
- [TONI] Marj!
- Yes, Toni?

167
00:07:16,894 --> 00:07:19,856
[TONI] Babe, how's our presentation
for LoveList going?

168
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:22,150
- The one for Ms. Lindsay?
- Hmm, yeah!

169
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:26,362
I'm currently working on it,
but I'm excited, Toni,

170
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:28,197
because I'm sure this is gonna be a hit.

171
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:31,242
[MARJ] I want it to be perfect.

172
00:07:31,325 --> 00:07:32,994
But, Toni, do you have any suggestions?

173
00:07:33,077 --> 00:07:36,330
Because I'm overthinking it.
I want it to be perfect.

174
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:39,125
[TONI] Sure, let me see.
Show me the preview first.

175
00:07:39,208 --> 00:07:41,544
[MARJ] Okay, here.
Maybe you have some suggestions.

176
00:07:41,627 --> 00:07:44,589
[TONI] Maybe make it a little darker.

177
00:07:44,672 --> 00:07:45,548
- [MARJ] Darker…
- [TONI] Yes.

178
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:47,008
- [MARJ] Red?
- [TONI] Then…

179
00:07:48,384 --> 00:07:50,011
Come on, Billy. Let's head to the canteen.

180
00:07:50,094 --> 00:07:51,888
I'll introduce you to Sir Eric.

181
00:07:51,971 --> 00:07:53,097
Okay.

182
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:55,016
[STUDENTS MURMURING INDISTINCTLY]

183
00:07:58,269 --> 00:07:59,437
[BOTH CHUCKLE SLIGHTLY]

184
00:08:00,021 --> 00:08:01,606
Looks like my enemies backed off, Billy.

185
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:03,274
Yeah. I wonder why.

186
00:08:03,357 --> 00:08:04,692
Maybe they're scared of you.

187
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:07,862
- Maybe they're scared of you.
- Me?! Do I look scary?

188
00:08:07,945 --> 00:08:09,280
- Very.
- Hey!

189
00:08:09,363 --> 00:08:12,492
Just kidding. [LAUGHS SLIGHTLY]
Just let me take boxing classes already.

190
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:14,577
I've been doing what you told me.

191
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:16,287
I've been avoiding trouble whenever I can.

192
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:18,748
- Mm-hmm!
- But they still bully me.

193
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:23,794
If any of them, or anyone else,
bullies you again,

194
00:08:23,878 --> 00:08:25,254
report it to me right away.

195
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:27,798
- Mm-hmm?
- Or to Sir Eric.

196
00:08:28,716 --> 00:08:29,926
Why Sir Eric?

197
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:33,012
Because he's here at school, Billy.

198
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:36,057
Ouch. That hurts.

199
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:37,975
- No, no, no! Sorry.
- Is she your big sister?

200
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:40,102
- No. You're my big sister.
- Shouldn't you tell me first?

201
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:41,687
- You should tell me first.
- [OLIVER] Okay.

202
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:43,105
[BILLY] Okay!

203
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:47,443
The parents really love our healthy meals.
They're so happy about them.

204
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:48,903
- [GASPS] Ma'am.
- [LUCY] Yes?

205
00:08:48,986 --> 00:08:50,321
Have you done the inventory yet?

206
00:08:50,404 --> 00:08:51,572
Ah, not yet.

207
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:52,865
I'll take care of it.

208
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:54,659
Oh, okay. Okay.

209
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:55,993
Good morning, Ms. Lucy.

210
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:57,745
[LUCY] Good morning! Good morning, Oliver.

211
00:08:57,828 --> 00:08:59,664
Good morning, Ma'am Lucy.

212
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:01,499
Uh, where's Sir Eric?

213
00:09:01,582 --> 00:09:03,834
He's out the back.
He's just taking care of something.

214
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:05,294
Hmm.

215
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:07,004
Do you need him?

216
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:07,922
Not really.

217
00:09:08,005 --> 00:09:10,675
Oliver just wanted
to give something to Sir Eric.

218
00:09:10,758 --> 00:09:11,759
[LUCY] Oh…

219
00:09:11,842 --> 00:09:15,763
I can just give Sir Eric
the food pack later.

220
00:09:15,846 --> 00:09:17,348
- You will? Okay.
- [OLIVER] Yes.

221
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:18,683
- Hmm.
- [LUCY CHUCKLES]

222
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:23,771
Oh, you changed the menu?

223
00:09:23,854 --> 00:09:25,398
Yes. Mm-hmm.

224
00:09:25,481 --> 00:09:30,444
You have salads now
and options for diabetic customers.

225
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:31,737
- Mm-hmm.
- That's amazing!

226
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:33,155
Who came up with that?

227
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:34,448
Eric did.

228
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:36,534
- [OLIVER] He's really amazing.
- Wow!

229
00:09:36,617 --> 00:09:38,077
[LUCY CHUCKLING]

230
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,829
[PHONE RINGING]

231
00:09:39,912 --> 00:09:41,455
- Ah, excuse me for a second.
- [LUCY] Okay.

232
00:09:42,164 --> 00:09:43,249
Hello?

233
00:09:43,749 --> 00:09:44,667
Yes, Charm?

234
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:47,253
Chief, I'm reviewing
Abi's resume right now.

235
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:50,631
I double-checked
the information she put here,

236
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:53,593
and it turns out she's lying to us.

237
00:09:53,676 --> 00:09:55,344
Lying? What do you mean?

238
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:58,723
The tech company she claimed
issued her IT certificate

239
00:09:58,806 --> 00:10:00,308
doesn't exist.

240
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:02,435
Okay. All right.

241
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:04,395
I'll handle it, Charm. Thank you.

242
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:09,692
[CHARM] Miss, one Americano, please.

243
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:11,527
- [BARISTA] Okay, it'll be ready in a bit.
- [CHARM] Thank you.

244
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:16,741
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

245
00:10:16,824 --> 00:10:18,618
[MUSIC FADES]

246
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:20,244
[OLIVER] It doesn't fit anymore.

247
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:22,038
[LUCY CHUCKLING]

248
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:24,373
Do you want me to call Eric?

249
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:26,542
Oh, no, it's okay.
I have to get back to the office.

250
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:28,210
- Oliver, I'll get going.
- Bye, Billy.

251
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,421
- Okay? Bye!
- Bye!

252
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:32,632
Hey, Eric.

253
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:34,634
- Oh?
- [LUCY] Oliver is here.

254
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:37,428
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

255
00:10:37,511 --> 00:10:39,305
- [OLIVER] Hello!
- Have you eaten yet?

256
00:10:39,388 --> 00:10:40,431
Yes!

257
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:44,268
[PHONE RINGING]

258
00:10:45,269 --> 00:10:46,270
Hello, dude.

259
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:47,855
Where are you?

260
00:10:47,938 --> 00:10:51,484
I just got to the prosecutor's office.

261
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:53,027
Are you okay?

262
00:10:55,237 --> 00:11:01,160
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

263
00:11:01,243 --> 00:11:02,703
[JORDAN SIGHS]

264
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:04,330
Don't worry about me.

265
00:11:04,413 --> 00:11:05,790
I got this.

266
00:11:05,873 --> 00:11:07,291
Good luck.

267
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,835
Sorry I can't be there with you.

268
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:12,463
I just have something I need
to take care of at the office.

269
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:15,633
I gotta go.

270
00:11:15,716 --> 00:11:18,344
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

271
00:11:18,427 --> 00:11:22,807
Abi, I had everything
on your resume verified,

272
00:11:23,724 --> 00:11:28,813
and we found out that
your IT certification is fake.

273
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:30,815
[TENSE MUSIC SWELLS]

274
00:11:30,898 --> 00:11:34,777
Pillar IT Certifications
is not a real company.

275
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:36,278
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

276
00:11:37,446 --> 00:11:39,323
Sorry, Ms. Billy.

277
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:43,494
I'm sorry I did that.

278
00:11:44,286 --> 00:11:45,955
I'm sorry that

279
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:47,706
I made it up.

280
00:11:49,041 --> 00:11:50,501
I only did it since

281
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:53,212
I don't have

282
00:11:53,295 --> 00:11:55,339
any formal training,

283
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:57,591
so I just put that I

284
00:11:57,675 --> 00:12:00,761
got a certificate online.

285
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:04,306
But Ms. Billy,
it's true that I did self-study

286
00:12:04,390 --> 00:12:07,143
because I have my own internet cafe.

287
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:11,147
I… I just really want to be
a part of LoveList.

288
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:15,443
So, Ms. Billy Idol, maybe

289
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:18,320
you can still consider me, please?

290
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:20,865
Abi, I also checked your other claims.

291
00:12:21,907 --> 00:12:24,952
I reached out to your last company,

292
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:28,122
and they mentioned that
you were involved in an accident.

293
00:12:28,205 --> 00:12:29,081
Uh…

294
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:32,793
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

295
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:34,086
Uh…

296
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:37,298
[SIGHS SHARPLY]

297
00:12:38,090 --> 00:12:40,801
Our house was destroyed in a fire.

298
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:43,179
They said that

299
00:12:44,221 --> 00:12:46,015
you died in that fire.

300
00:12:46,098 --> 00:12:50,060
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

301
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:51,312
[INHALES SHARPLY]

302
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,481
Um…

303
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:57,651
Ms. Billy, that…

304
00:12:57,735 --> 00:12:59,153
that wasn't me.

305
00:12:59,236 --> 00:13:00,237
Um…

306
00:13:00,321 --> 00:13:01,530
They got it wrong.

307
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:04,074
They… they got it all wrong.

308
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:07,578
They thought it was me,
but I wasn't the one who died.

309
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:09,455
It was my sister.

310
00:13:09,538 --> 00:13:11,457
It was my sister who died, not me.

311
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:16,420
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

312
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:20,174
[CRYING]

313
00:13:29,099 --> 00:13:31,185
It wasn't me who died.

314
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:33,896
It was my sister.

315
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:38,400
It was my fault too.

316
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:42,363
I never went back to the company
to explain myself

317
00:13:42,446 --> 00:13:46,867
because my sister had just died,

318
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:50,371
and I had to take care of my mother.

319
00:13:50,454 --> 00:13:54,583
I couldn't explain myself
because I was a mess.

320
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:57,795
My mind was such
a mess back then, Ms. Billy.

321
00:13:57,878 --> 00:14:01,840
[CRYING]

322
00:14:02,841 --> 00:14:06,011
Abi, as much as I would love to help you…

323
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:11,934
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

324
00:14:12,017 --> 00:14:13,644
…I cannot hire you.

325
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:15,854
Ms. Billy…

326
00:14:17,106 --> 00:14:19,441
Let me help you
in a different way instead.

327
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:21,819
There is no other way, Ms. Billy, please.

328
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:24,238
Please, Ms. Billy.

329
00:14:24,321 --> 00:14:27,992
- Please, please, Ms. Billy.
- Abi…

330
00:14:28,075 --> 00:14:31,579
Please, let me apply.
I'll take any position, please!

331
00:14:31,662 --> 00:14:33,664
- [BILLY] Abi…
- I'll take any position!

332
00:14:33,747 --> 00:14:36,208
I really need the money
for my mother's medical expenses.

333
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:38,210
- Stand up, Abi.
- Please.

334
00:14:38,294 --> 00:14:40,504
Please, please, please, please.

335
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:42,631
Then why did you lie?

336
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:46,427
You know you're good, Abi.

337
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:49,638
You even proved that
you were qualified during the interview.

338
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:51,473
You answered everything!

339
00:14:53,392 --> 00:14:56,520
But do you know the one thing
I can't stand in a colleague?

340
00:14:57,813 --> 00:14:59,565
Liars.

341
00:15:02,276 --> 00:15:05,112
Abi, I need someone I can trust.

342
00:15:05,195 --> 00:15:10,743
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

343
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:29,845
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

344
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:33,933
So, for the record, Mr. Toledo,

345
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:36,852
you admit that you stabbed Mr. Valentin.

346
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:39,188
- [GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]
- Yes…

347
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:41,649
But I never did that

348
00:15:42,566 --> 00:15:44,693
trying to hurt Sir Jordan,

349
00:15:45,819 --> 00:15:47,071
let alone kill him.

350
00:15:47,154 --> 00:15:49,823
I may look like a killer,
but I would never kill anyone.

351
00:15:50,908 --> 00:15:52,368
I did it because…

352
00:15:53,994 --> 00:15:55,746
I just wanted to scare him.

353
00:15:55,829 --> 00:15:57,039
That's all.

354
00:15:57,122 --> 00:16:00,668
So you're no longer claiming self-defense?

355
00:16:01,418 --> 00:16:03,379
This is different from your testimony.

356
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:06,799
Yes.

357
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:09,593
Why did you change your testimony?

358
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:12,179
Because I know it was wrong.

359
00:16:13,263 --> 00:16:14,640
I regret what I did.

360
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:17,184
Please forgive me, Sir Jordan.

361
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:19,728
I'd like to apologize to them.

362
00:16:19,812 --> 00:16:22,022
[FISCAL] So are you willing
to state for the record

363
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:24,024
that you forgive him

364
00:16:24,108 --> 00:16:26,318
and you no longer
wish to pursue this complaint?

365
00:16:26,402 --> 00:16:27,569
No.

366
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:30,614
I want him to go to jail.

367
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:34,284
Not just for what he did to me,

368
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:37,663
but for what he did to my friend.

369
00:16:37,746 --> 00:16:38,956
To our company.

370
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:42,710
He threatened. Harassed.

371
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:45,254
He tried to ruin everything we built!

372
00:16:45,337 --> 00:16:48,048
So I want him

373
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:49,174
to go to jail.

374
00:16:49,258 --> 00:16:50,884
Sir, please forgive me!

375
00:16:51,468 --> 00:16:53,095
Sir Jordan, please forgive me!

376
00:16:53,178 --> 00:16:54,013
I…

377
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:55,681
I was just following orders!

378
00:16:55,764 --> 00:16:58,559
Who gave you those orders?

379
00:17:00,936 --> 00:17:01,979
[MARJ] Chief?

380
00:17:02,062 --> 00:17:04,732
Chief, I already sent
the revised LoveFeast deck.

381
00:17:04,815 --> 00:17:06,567
Please let me know what else you need.

382
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:09,111
I already saved it to my hard drive.

383
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:12,740
Okay. Thank you, Marj.

384
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:14,700
[MARJ] Okay. Thank you.

385
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,372
I already informed the chief.
Let's take a break.

386
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:21,999
[WOMAN] Break? Let's go!

387
00:17:22,082 --> 00:17:28,839
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

388
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:41,602
Just say it so we can put an end to this.

389
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:44,229
Caloy!

390
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:46,398
Shirley De Leon!

391
00:17:46,482 --> 00:17:49,443
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

392
00:17:50,027 --> 00:17:52,446
She used to be a LoveList employee, right?

393
00:17:54,114 --> 00:17:56,283
She's the one who has a grudge
against Ma'am Billy.

394
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:00,996
The accountant?

395
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,372
Yes.

396
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:04,500
That's right, Sir Jordan. The accountant.

397
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:06,919
Ma'am Billy fired her because…

398
00:18:08,504 --> 00:18:10,297
she stole money from the company.

399
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:13,300
She already apologized,

400
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:15,344
but Ma'am Billy pushed through
with the case.

401
00:18:15,427 --> 00:18:18,555
That's why Ma'am Shirley
is holding a grudge against her.

402
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:21,141
- Are you kidding me, Caloy?!
- [FISCAL] Mr. Valentin!

403
00:18:21,225 --> 00:18:23,894
I would advise you to proceed calmly.

404
00:18:23,977 --> 00:18:27,564
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

405
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:36,406
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

406
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:40,828
[FIRE ALARM BLARING]

407
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:43,747
[ABI] Oh no, there's a fire!
Can't you hear the alarm?!

408
00:18:45,499 --> 00:18:46,542
Run! Hurry!

409
00:18:47,084 --> 00:18:48,043
Hurry!

410
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:49,878
Where's the fire starting?!

411
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:56,468
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

412
00:18:57,052 --> 00:19:00,013
- What's going on?
- I don't know.

413
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:02,349
Girls? Girls!

414
00:19:02,432 --> 00:19:03,517
Please, don't panic.

415
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,477
Let's exit calmly, okay?

416
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:07,563
Let's go, I'll meet you outside.

417
00:19:07,646 --> 00:19:08,939
Okay. Thank you.

418
00:19:09,022 --> 00:19:10,732
[FIRE ALARM CONTINUES BLARING]

419
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:11,942
Why did the alarm go off?

420
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:13,360
Security is checking it now.

421
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:15,028
- [BLAIRE] Oh my God!
- Let's go, girls.

422
00:19:15,112 --> 00:19:17,614
- There's a fire!
- [TONI] Slowly!

423
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:19,241
Blaire, make sure no one's left behind.

424
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:20,492
[BLAIRE] Yes, your bag is with me.

425
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:21,952
Go. Be careful.

426
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:28,083
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC
CONTINUES, FADES]

427
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:29,877
[BILLY] Is there anyone left inside?

428
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,461
- [WOMAN 1] I don't think so.
- All right.

429
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:33,380
Chief, it was a false alarm.

430
00:19:33,463 --> 00:19:35,048
It was a waste of energy.

431
00:19:35,132 --> 00:19:37,009
- Geez, I'm exhausted!
- [BILLY] What?

432
00:19:37,092 --> 00:19:40,095
Ma'am, negative on the fire incident.
We already inspected the area.

433
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:44,057
It could have been a malfunction
or an accident that triggered the alarm.

434
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:45,893
[BILLY] Ah, okay.

435
00:19:46,393 --> 00:19:47,853
Glad to hear that.

436
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:49,771
Okay, girls? Did you hear that?

437
00:19:49,855 --> 00:19:51,982
I'm sorry, it was a false alarm.

438
00:19:52,065 --> 00:19:54,735
We can go back inside.
Let's get back to work!

439
00:19:54,818 --> 00:19:56,737
Sorry for the hassle.
All right, come on in.

440
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:58,197
[WOMAN] Let's go.

441
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,448
I'm sorry!

442
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:01,617
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

443
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:02,659
Are you okay?

444
00:20:03,994 --> 00:20:05,037
Abi!

445
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:07,664
Ms. Billy.

446
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:09,625
Hey. You're still here.

447
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:11,877
Ah, yes. But I'm about to leave.

448
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:15,339
Ah… Ms. Billy.

449
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:18,091
Uh… I'm really sorry

450
00:20:18,175 --> 00:20:20,469
that I lied.

451
00:20:20,552 --> 00:20:23,055
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

452
00:20:23,138 --> 00:20:27,851
Even though I can't work here in LoveList,

453
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:29,811
I just want you to know that

454
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:32,522
I still idolize you.

455
00:20:34,191 --> 00:20:36,026
Thank you, Abi.

456
00:20:37,819 --> 00:20:44,826
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

457
00:20:48,413 --> 00:20:49,289
Good luck, okay?

458
00:20:52,584 --> 00:20:53,835
- See you.
- Take care.

459
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:02,261
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

460
00:21:02,344 --> 00:21:04,721
So, that's the end of my presentation!

461
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:06,098
[CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]

462
00:21:06,181 --> 00:21:07,182
What do you think, chief?

463
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:11,061
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

464
00:21:11,144 --> 00:21:12,938
[BLAIRE] Excuse me. Chief?

465
00:21:13,021 --> 00:21:14,398
- Chief.
- [BILLY] Yes?

466
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:16,692
Ms. Lindsay's secretary called.

467
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:19,736
She wants to reschedule
because of a family emergency.

468
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:22,572
Okay. Then let's resched the meeting.

469
00:21:22,656 --> 00:21:24,783
We still need to change things up, anyway.

470
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:26,118
Okay.

471
00:21:26,201 --> 00:21:28,370
So you don't approve of this?

472
00:21:28,453 --> 00:21:30,580
I don't know.
Seems like something is missing.

473
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:31,665
Like a piece of the puzzle.

474
00:21:32,666 --> 00:21:33,750
Oh…

475
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:38,463
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

476
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:40,048
[MUSIC FADES]

477
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:41,425
[TERE] Hurry, get them out.

478
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:43,802
Come back once you're done.
There's still a bunch more stuff here.

479
00:21:43,885 --> 00:21:45,095
Ms. Tere!

480
00:21:45,178 --> 00:21:46,221
[TERE SCOFFS]

481
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,931
Put it down, and be gentle! Ms. Tere!

482
00:21:48,015 --> 00:21:49,266
- What now, huh?!
- Ms. Tere!

483
00:21:49,349 --> 00:21:50,809
You said one week!

484
00:21:50,892 --> 00:21:53,270
Well, a week has already passed!

485
00:21:53,353 --> 00:21:54,771
Where will I store my computers?

486
00:21:54,855 --> 00:21:56,940
- They'll be damaged outside!
- [CHUCKLES DRYLY]

487
00:21:57,024 --> 00:22:00,861
Then sell them
to cover part of what you owe me!

488
00:22:00,944 --> 00:22:02,863
Ms. Tere, so much has
already happened today!

489
00:22:02,946 --> 00:22:05,032
Please, don't make it worse!

490
00:22:05,115 --> 00:22:06,867
It's been one bad thing after another!

491
00:22:06,950 --> 00:22:09,703
That's not my problem!
I already have a lot on my plate!

492
00:22:09,786 --> 00:22:11,413
What, you think you're my only problem?

493
00:22:11,496 --> 00:22:13,248
We struck a deal!

494
00:22:13,332 --> 00:22:14,666
You promised to pay after a week!

495
00:22:14,750 --> 00:22:17,586
Keep this up,
and you'll get nowhere in life!

496
00:22:17,669 --> 00:22:19,463
- [ABI SNARLS]
- [TERE SCREAMS]

497
00:22:19,546 --> 00:22:22,257
- [CALOY] Abi! Abi, Abi!
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

498
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:23,216
Abi.

499
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:26,136
[TERE WAILING]

500
00:22:26,219 --> 00:22:27,137
[BAG THUDS]

501
00:22:29,222 --> 00:22:30,599
[KEEPS WAILING]

502
00:22:41,234 --> 00:22:43,528
[ABI] <i>That Billy</i>
<i>is so greedy!</i>

503
00:22:43,612 --> 00:22:47,157
<i>All I'm asking for is a job.</i>
<i>But she can't even give me that?!</i>

504
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:49,993
<i>You want to study at</i>
<i>the University of Kingsley, right?</i>

505
00:22:50,077 --> 00:22:51,203
[OLIVER]
<i>I'd rather go to the US.</i>

506
00:22:51,286 --> 00:22:53,080
<i>My sister said</i>
<i>our father's grave is there.</i>

507
00:22:53,163 --> 00:22:57,292
<i>Second chances are a gift,</i>
<i>not an obligation.</i>

508
00:22:57,375 --> 00:22:59,127
<i>Give it when you're ready.</i>

509
00:22:59,211 --> 00:23:01,838
<i>Do you really believe</i>
<i>what you said earlier?</i>

510
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:03,673
<i>Second chances</i>
<i>could be earned?</i>

511
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:05,175
<i>About your dad.</i>

512
00:23:05,258 --> 00:23:06,843
<i>Let me ask you</i>
<i>the same thing.</i>

513
00:23:06,927 --> 00:23:08,512
<i>Do you have it in you</i>
<i>to forgive?</i>

514
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:11,640
<i>Dear? Please, let's talk.</i>
